  {
   "id": "syn-nvda-1",
   "text": "Nvidia said on Wednesday that demand for its data centre chips continued to exceed what it can ship, and raised its revenue forecast for the current quarter above analysts' estimates.\n\nThe company reported quarterly revenue up sharply from a year earlier, led by sales of accelerators to cloud providers building out capacity for artificial intelligence workloads. Gross margin widened as the mix shifted toward its newest products.\n\nThe chief financial officer said supply constraints would ease gradually through the year as a second packaging partner comes on line, but that visibility into orders now extends several quarters.\n\nShares rose in extended trading. Analysts noted that the forecast implies continued growth in capital spending by the largest cloud customers, though several flagged that customer concentration remains a risk.",
   "context": "article",
   "source": {
    "title": "Nvidia raises outlook as data centre orders outrun supply",
